1. WHAT YOU MAY DO
   a. Read, study and compile the source code for Your own use.
   b. Modify the source code for Your own use and run the modified program.
   c. Use the Software (official release builds, or builds You compile) to
      create Your Works, for personal and commercial purposes, without paying
      the Licensor any royalty on Your Works.
   d. Make copies of the Software for backup, and install it on the computers
      that You personally own or control.
   e. Share small excerpts of the source code in bug reports, security
      reports and pull requests sent to the Licensor.

2. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO
   a. Distribute, sell, rent, lend, sublicense or publish the Software, in
      whole or in part, in source or binary form, including modified versions,
      except as section 1.e allows.
   b. Publish or distribute a fork, a derivative program or a competing product
      that contains code from the Software.
   c. Remove or change copyright, licence or attribution notices.
   d. Use the Licensor's name, the name "Jank!" or its logos for another
      product or in a way that suggests the Licensor endorses it.
   e. Use the Software to train or build a competing product, or to offer the
      Software, or access to it, as a service to others.

3. YOUR WORKS
   Your Works belong to You. The Software adds no watermark and the Licensor
   claims no rights over Your Works. Project files (.jank) store only Your
   content and the settings needed to open it.

4. BUNDLED ASSETS
   Pictures, models and fonts that ship with the Software (splash screens,
   the butterfly model and texture, the demo project and others) are
   licensed only for use inside the Software and for viewing the demo. They
   may not be extracted and redistributed on their own, unless the file
   THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt says otherwise for that item. If You use a bundled
   asset inside Your Works (for example the butterfly primitive in a game),
   You may do so as part of Your Works.

5. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
   The Software contains open-source components that keep their own licences.
   They are listed in app/assets/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt and in the program
   under Help > Licences. Nothing in this agreement limits Your rights under
